{
  "requirement": "For node reads, the SDK constructs a `Snapshot` from\nthe contents returned by `Domain::node_content` and their\n`NodeContents::fingerprint` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.fingerprint`, without another read.\n\n```rust,ignore\n#[non_exhaustive]\npub struct Snapshot<T> {\n    pub content: T,\n    pub fingerprint: Fingerprint,\n}\n\nimpl<T> Snapshot<T> {\n    pub fn new(content: T, fingerprint: Fingerprint) -> Self;\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl<T: Clone> Clone for Snapshot<T>;\nimpl<T: Debug> Debug for Snapshot<T>;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.graph.snapshot`.\n\n**Obligations and the tests that cover them**\n- **The `Snapshot::new` constructor and public fields.**\n  - `tests/contracts.rs#fn[callers_can_pair_content_with_its_fingerprint]` builds a `Snapshot` with `Snapshot::new`.\n  - It asserts that `content` and `fingerprint` hold the supplied values.\n- **Node reads build the snapshot from `Domain::node_content` and its `NodeContents::fingerprint`.**\n  - `validation_tests.rs#fn[direct_reads_return_complete_unicode_contents_and_snapshots]` calls `read_snapshot`. It uses an empty string and a large multi-byte Unicode string.\n  - It asserts that `snapshot.fingerprint` equals the expected fingerprint of the stored contents.\n  - It asserts that the content formats back to the original. It also checks that the recorded dependency carries the same fingerprint.\n  - `validation_tests.rs#fn[snapshots_record_exact_reads_and_retain_distinct_versions]` asserts the fingerprint from `read_snapshot` for \"before\". It then changes the node and checks that the earlier and later reads keep distinct fingerprints.\n  - The agent tests in `agent/tests.rs` (`graph_tools_record_delivered_snapshots_and_prepared_pages_do_not_record_delivery`) assert `Dependency::Node` fingerprints from `read_node`.\n- **\"Without another read\".**\n  - `contracts.rs#fn[identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot]` reads one snapshot and then mutates the underlying node.\n  - It asserts that `snapshot.content.fingerprint() == snapshot.fingerprint`. It also asserts that the content still formats as \"before\", that the fingerprint value is \"before\", and that the domain's `reads` is exactly `[1]`.\n  - A second read or a recomputation against fresh state would break one of these assertions.\n  - `validation_tests.rs#fn[snapshots_record_exact_reads_and_retain_distinct_versions]` asserts the exact read log `[1, 1, 1, 2]`. `direct_reads_return_complete_unicode_contents_and_snapshots` asserts `[1, 1]`.\n- **Failed reads produce no snapshot.** A missing node returns an error and records no dependency. This is asserted in both `snapshots_record_exact_reads_and_retain_distinct_versions` and `direct_reads_return_complete_unicode_contents_and_snapshots`.\n- **Fingerprint semantics under `requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.fingerprint`.** `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[requirement_edges_and_input_freshness_use_the_sdk]` checks two things for the Habeas domain's contents. A fingerprint already taken stays the same after the files change. A freshly read fingerprint differs after the change. This covers a cited requirement as it applies here.\n\n**Items not requiring a dedicated test**\n- `Clone` and `Debug` for `Snapshot` are `#[derive(Clone, Debug)]` on the struct in `graph.rs`. They have no conditional or transformation of their own.\n- `#[non_exhaustive]` and the public shape are type-level declarations. `public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` checks the export inventory.\n\nI found no unacknowledged gap.",
